  "method": {
    "commandVM": "cargo build --manifest-path mixer/vm/Cargo.toml --locked --offline --release --features experimental-guest-ui-v2-native -j 1",
    "commandSwift": "swift build --build-tests --package-path storage-test --scratch-path swift-build -j 3 with the pinned stage 4 transport, host bridge and HostEntry, VM headers and probed dylib",
    "commandSigned": "xctest -XCTest ChecklistTests.ChecklistTitleTests/testSignedTitleFirstFrameAndRollback <ChecklistTests.xctest>",
    "signedRuns": "Five paired original/rebuilt macOS XCTest processes in alternating order. Each uses fresh private workspace/recovery directories and both title sizes with sequence 1, sequence 2, sequence 3 and cold reopen. Same signed material checks and real workspace repository. Display acknowledgement is synthetic as in the handed XCTest.",
    "directRuns": "Two 192-journey native FFI sweeps of the exact reviewed Wasm pair. Each sweeps 32 times through 62-byte, escaped 240-byte, and same-length 240-byte ASCII titles. Replays complete/open, review, confirm and real VM wake turns with trusted synthetic storage completions, checking exact frame bytes and state. The second sweep reverses packet order each round.",
    "titles": "Same 62- and 240-byte fixture suffixes as the handed XCTest, with fixed 36-byte UUID-shaped prefixes for cross-packet byte equality. Original fixture used fresh random UUID-shaped prefixes.",
    "turnProbe": "Windows start at the Instant used to calculate the 50 ms deadline in CapabilityGuest::run. They end at the first observed failed deadline check or successful return from finish_turn. Probe reads Darwin CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID, counts guest imports and emits a record after measuring. No interpreter deadline, mailbox deadline, signed limits, fuel or validation threshold was modified.",
    "admissionProbe": "Signed elapsed wall measures beginDownload through finishDownload before start. Direct elapsed wall and same-thread CPU include VM structural validation and session creation before the first turn.",
    "limits": "No scheduler trace distinguishes preemption from other off-CPU stalls. The earlier exact historical host location was not instrumented. Natural host load, no artificial stress treatment. Per-operation counts are descriptive, not a comparative failure-rate estimate."
